<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Theodosia</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 355 BCE (approx.) · capital Theodosia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Milesian port in south-eastern Crimea that exported grain until it was conquered by the Bosporan Kingdom in the 4th century BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Theodosia</a> was founded by settlers from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/miletus">Miletus</a> in the 6th century BCE on a bay of the south-eastern Crimean coast, at modern Feodosia. Its good harbour and fertile hinterland made it an important outlet for grain grown by local peoples.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Theodosia</a> lived from exporting grain, fish and hides to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>, especially <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a>. It long resisted absorption by the neighbouring <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bosporan-kingdom">Bosporan Kingdom</a>, with help from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/heraclea-pontica">Heraclea Pontica</a>. The Bosporan ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satyrus-i">Satyrus I</a> died while besieging it in 389 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leucon-i">Leucon I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bosporan-kingdom">Bosporan Kingdom</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Theodosia</a>, probably c. 355 BCE, and developed its harbour for the grain trade with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a>. It remained a Bosporan city and centuries later became the Genoese port of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaffa">Kaffa</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 600 BCE – 355 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">ci